135
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:35,440
Scoutmastership in seven minutes or less.

136
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:48,280
You know, early on when I became Scoutmaster, I found myself yelling at my scouts.

137
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:50,800
Do you find yourself yelling at your scouts?

138
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:54,840
How about your youth leadership? or your fellow scouts?

139
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:57,680
Oh yeah, I've been there.

140
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:03,440
I know that sometimes things get frustrating or sometimes you have to get attention,

141
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:10,200
but yelling is really kind of an aggressive, authoritarian leadership thing. right,

142
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:14,080
It gets compliance, but it doesn't really get anything else.

143
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:19,000
I'm a big guy, especially when it comes to you know, in comparison with my scouts,

144
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:24,120
I can loom and I can be very intimidating,

145
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:28,080
And if I raise my voice that's doubly intimidating.

146
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:32,600
But raising my voice does not earn me respect, not at all.

147
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:36,120
It makes me into someone who's feared and disliked.

148
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:41,160
I mean, it's the lowest form of leadership, if you can even call it leadership,

149
00:10:41,160 --> 00:10:44,600
And it reminds me of something that Baden Powell said in one of his writings.

150
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:47,400
He said: any ass can be a commander,

151
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:50,400
And I don't even have to comment on that.

152
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:53,040
I mean he had it down right.

153
00:10:53,079 --> 00:10:57,520
There's a big difference between speaking loudly and yelling,

154
00:10:57,520 --> 00:11:02,959
And let's define yelling as raising your voice and frustration or anger.

155
00:11:02,959 --> 00:11:07,160
Now, speaking loudly is asking everybody to volunteer their attention,

156
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:10,160
And in scouting sometimes you're going to raise your voice

157
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:14,880
And you can do that in a friendly, kind and courteous attitude,

158
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:17,520
Something you can't do when you're yelling.

159
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:20,480
A lot of times you'll be able to use the convention of holding up the scout

160
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:23,040
sign and getting everybody's attention.

161
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:25,440
But if you're in a campsite or something like that,

162
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:29,000
or everybody's all spread out, sometimes you may have to raise your voice.

163
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:34,440
But we don't want to train our scouts to only respond to an adult

164
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:37,280
or a youth leader who yells.

165
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:41,520
And we don't yell at scouts because we have a much bigger job to do

166
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:44,920
than merely making them compliant. right,

167
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:48,240
We want good group discipline and that comes from a combination

168
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:50,480
of citizenship and loyalty,

169
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:55,160
And I think that's best developed in an atmosphere of voluntary obedience,

170
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:59,600
not obedience compelled by the threat of punishment or being yelled at.

171
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:01,840
Here's what I tell my youth leaders. right,

172
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:05,280
If the scouts are all distracted and squirrely and you need your attention,

173
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:08,440
you ask for their attention once and then you wait

174
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:12,880
If they don't respond right away- and they hardly ever do.

175
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:14,280
you just continue waiting.

176
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:17,240
This is what I tell my youth leaders. okay,

177
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:20,240
And let's. we're at a troop meeting, we're in a campsite,

178
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:24,240
we're in any situation. they need to get the attention of the guys

179
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:26,800
and their patrol. or maybe the senior patrol leader

180
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:28,880
needs to get the attention of the troop.

181
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:31,280
And you know a couple of guys, just

182
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:33,200
he just can't break through.

183
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:35,160
So I say you go and ask them this question:

184
00:12:35,160 --> 00:12:37,320
Can you get with the program here

185
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:39,760
or do you need to go talk to the scout master?

186
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:42,560
So give them a choice. right,

187
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:44,240
They can get with what you're doing

188
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:45,900
or they can come and talk to me.

189
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:49,060
Any scout who gets referred to the scout master

190
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:50,540
gets to talk to me.

191
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:52,220
And if that same scout needs to come over

192
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:55,459
and talk to me on a regular basis about this,

193
00:12:55,459 --> 00:12:57,699
well then we're gonna be getting their parents involved

194
00:12:57,699 --> 00:12:59,660
and we're gonna be talking to them too.

195
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:02,459
But this discussion with your youth leaders

196
00:13:02,459 --> 00:13:04,420
would help set the way forward.

197
00:13:04,420 --> 00:13:07,520
You work together to arrive at an agreement

198
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:11,380
that nobody- no adult and no youth leader-

199
00:13:11,380 --> 00:13:14,220
ever yells at anyone for any reason.

200
00:13:14,220 --> 00:13:15,260
And once you've done this,

201
00:13:15,260 --> 00:13:18,939
once you've kind of declared a yell-free zone

202
00:13:18,939 --> 00:13:21,020
with your patrol leader's counsel,

203
00:13:21,020 --> 00:13:23,500
then you may wanna make sure to share that with the scouts

204
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:25,300
so that they all understand,

205
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:27,580
And you wanna make sure to share that with the other adults.

206
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:29,380
This is a yell-free zone.

207
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:30,580
We're drawing a line

208
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:32,660
Now. if you make a bunch of rules,

209
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:36,140
you'll have to break them, make an agreement right

210
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:37,340
And then work within it

211
00:13:37,340 --> 00:13:39,300
to best serve each individual scout.

212
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:42,060
Most of us have at least a couple of scouts

213
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:45,020
who are gonna find it really difficult to stay focused

214
00:13:45,140 --> 00:13:48,699
And they may benefit from a little counseling now again,

215
00:13:48,699 --> 00:13:51,140
They may need a little more leeway

216
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:52,699
as they start to get the handle

217
00:13:52,699 --> 00:13:55,340
on their ability to concentrate or follow.

218
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:57,420
If you have a yelling problem in your troop,

219
00:13:57,420 --> 00:13:58,660
look at the situations

220
00:13:58,660 --> 00:14:00,819
that commonly cause people to yell.

221
00:14:00,819 --> 00:14:04,500
It may be that you're painting yourself into a corner right.

222
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:07,020
Watch for situations where someone has to demand

223
00:14:07,020 --> 00:14:09,340
the intention of the entire troop.

224
00:14:09,340 --> 00:14:11,660
Scouting really doesn't work on that scale.

225
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:13,740
It's not designed to work on that scale.

226
00:14:13,740 --> 00:14:15,860
It works on the scale of the patrol.

227
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:19,140
90% of the time a scout should be under the direction

228
00:14:19,140 --> 00:14:20,460
of his patrol leader,

229
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:23,660
not just another face in a larger crowd.

230
00:14:23,660 --> 00:14:26,060
And, as I've said many times,

231
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:29,660
we need to be careful about who dispenses discipline.

232
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:31,260
Youth leaders refer scouts

233
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:33,020
to the scout master for correction.

234
00:14:33,020 --> 00:14:34,380
They never punish,

235
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:35,860
They don't yell at scouts,

236
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:37,420
They don't apply any aggressive,

237
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:39,780
authoritarian methods of discipline,

238
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:42,460
because scouts are boys,

239
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:45,540
and boys this age tend to go all Lord of the Flies

240
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:46,380
pretty quickly.

