283
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:06,060
I just sent out one of the weekly troop emails

284
00:17:06,060 --> 00:17:08,060
that parents and committee members

285
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:10,060
tell me they really appreciate.

286
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:12,060
It reminds them of the troop meeting,

287
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:14,060
upcoming campout, other special events,

288
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:15,060
things like that.

289
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:18,060
Now I'm feeling a little conflicted about doing this

290
00:17:18,060 --> 00:17:20,060
because I would really rather

291
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:22,060
that the Scouts took care of this themselves

292
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:25,060
and that they wanted to know and ask questions

293
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:28,060
than me spoon-feeding them all this information

294
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:30,060
through this newsletter.

295
00:17:30,060 --> 00:17:32,060
If I stop sending the newsletter,

296
00:17:32,060 --> 00:17:34,060
my committee is not going to be happy.

297
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:37,060
I'll stop in arms already about the changes we're making

298
00:17:37,060 --> 00:17:39,060
And I'm looking for a little advice about this.

299
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:42,060
Well, Bill, I get what you're saying about the newsletter,

300
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:44,060
but I don't think it's at cross purposes

301
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:47,060
with developing what you want to see in your youth leaders.

302
00:17:47,060 --> 00:17:50,060
There's apples and oranges that we're dealing with here:

303
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:53,060
keeping parents and committee members informed

304
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:55,060
and having Scouts develop some leadership

305
00:17:55,060 --> 00:17:56,060
and discovery skills.

306
00:17:56,060 --> 00:18:00,060
Those are really kind of two separate things.

307
00:18:00,060 --> 00:18:03,060
So as Scoutmasters we need to be rigidly flexible

308
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:05,060
and not too dogmatic.

309
00:18:05,060 --> 00:18:08,060
One way to blend the apples and oranges in this situation

310
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:10,060
is maybe involving the Patrol Leaders Council

311
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:13,060
in helping you create that email newsletter. right,

312
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:15,060
But this is fraught with dangers

313
00:18:15,060 --> 00:18:17,060
because if you totally hand it off to them,

314
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:20,060
it's going to become a writing assignment in their minds

315
00:18:20,060 --> 00:18:22,060
and it's not going to go very far.

316
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:24,060
if you're a Scouts or anything like mine,

317
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:27,060
The best way, I think, is for you to collect their thoughts

318
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:30,060
and plans and translate them for the adults,

319
00:18:30,060 --> 00:18:32,060
their parents and the committee members

320
00:18:32,060 --> 00:18:34,060
through your newsletter,

321
00:18:34,060 --> 00:18:36,060
which is probably what you're doing anyway.

322
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:38,060
It takes a lot of effort for any of us

323
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:40,060
to get a perspective on Scouting

324
00:18:40,060 --> 00:18:43,060
that allows youth leadership

325
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:46,060
to actually have real responsibility,

326
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:48,060
And once you have that perspective,

327
00:18:48,060 --> 00:18:50,060
you can help other people gain it

328
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:53,060
by translating what you see your Scouts doing

329
00:18:53,060 --> 00:18:57,060
into something cogent for their families to understand.

330
00:18:57,060 --> 00:19:00,060
Youth leaders, in my experience,

331
00:19:00,060 --> 00:19:04,060
do not make those translations as well as you can.

332
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:07,060
They don't get into adult speak very well

333
00:19:07,060 --> 00:19:09,060
and it's kind of distracting to ask them to do so

334
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:11,060
because they're busy doing other things.

335
00:19:11,060 --> 00:19:14,060
Guide them through the discovery process

336
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:17,060
and then translate their conclusions into the newsletter.

337
00:19:17,060 --> 00:19:20,060
Now, at the same time, I would offer to include

338
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:22,060
anything that they would like to write,

339
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:26,060
but I wouldn't necessarily make that an assignment.

340
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:28,060
You'll probably end up discovering a Scout

341
00:19:28,060 --> 00:19:30,060
who shows some talent for this,

342
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:33,060
So you encourage it and capitalize on it.

343
00:19:33,060 --> 00:19:35,060
I've had Scouts who were very, very good

344
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:37,060
at writing- you know- information

345
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:39,060
for the newsletter or emails

346
00:19:39,060 --> 00:19:41,060
and who really enjoyed doing that.

347
00:19:41,060 --> 00:19:43,060
But sometimes they don't

348
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:46,060
and that's a great thing to capitalize on.

349
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:49,060
So, in the end, keep sending out the newsletter-

350
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:51,060
It's a great idea.

351
00:19:51,060 --> 00:19:53,060
Keep encouraging your youth leaders

352
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:56,060
to ask questions and find things out for themselves,

353
00:19:56,060 --> 00:19:58,060
But remember that keeping parents informed,

354
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:00,060
keeping your committee informed

355
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:04,060
and having your Scouts really value that discovery process-

356
00:20:04,060 --> 00:20:06,060
they can be two different things.

357
00:20:06,060 --> 00:20:08,060
Bill had another question in that email

